  "solution": {
    "text": "In the given circuit, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> are at the same potential. Points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> are also at the same potential.<br /><br />Therefore, the resistance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> will be ineffective and neglected. Now, the circuit becomes<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/rrfnkkbsagtefmfsayzumpszokerybuufogveukbbajtyzdbqx.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 145px; width: 200px;\" /><br /><br />In the above circuit, branch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCD</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AEFD</mi></math> are in the parallel combination.<br /><br />Thus, the net resistance of the circuit.<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Current, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.33</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
